Name: toolbarHidden

Type: message

Syntax: toolbarHidden

Summary:
Sent to the current card when a toolbar becomes hidden.

Associations: card

Introduced: 9.7.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
on toolbarHidden
  set the height of card field "content" to the height of this card
end toolbarHidden

Example:
-- Stack script: keep layout in sync with toolbar visibility
on toolbarShown
  updateLayout
end toolbarShown

on toolbarHidden
  updateLayout
end toolbarHidden

on updateLayout
  local tUsable
  put the height of this card - the toolbarHeight into tUsable
  set the height of card field "main" to tUsable
end updateLayout

Description:
The <toolbarHidden> message is sent to the current card whenever the
stack's toolbar becomes hidden — either because a script sets the
<toolbarVisible> property to false, or because the stack is opened with
the toolbar already hidden.

On Mac the toolbar lives above the card area, so the card's usable height
is unaffected. On Windows and Linux the toolbar occupies space inside the
card area, so handlers should adjust the layout of controls accordingly.
The <toolbarHeight> function returns the current height of the toolbar and
returns 0 when it is hidden.

The message is sent before any visual update, so changes made in the
handler take effect in the same refresh cycle.

References: toolbarShown (message), toolbarVisible (property),
toolbarHeight (function), toolbar (object)

Tags: ui
